      "body": "## Motivation\n\nRemove a redundant host collective from eligible eager decoder replay tails by reusing DP token counts already exchanged during synchronized DSPARK prefill.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add count reuse for CUDA MegaMoE + DSPARK with speculative prefill coordination disabled, attention TP=CP=1, and complete early/late count vectors.\n- Preserve existing eligibility checks and the collective fallback for all other configurations or incomplete metadata.\n- Change one Python helper; graph-owned count buffers remain unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Reported local eligibility/fallback checks and pre-commit passed. Observation-only prefill/idle probes found no count mismatches.\n- GSM8K (200 examples, baseline/reuse/reuse/baseline): **197/195/197/197** correct.\n- First tokens matched across ten directed inputs. Top-20 logprobs varied even between baseline restarts, so numerical equivalence remains unestablished.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nReported fixed-batch prefill measurements with the Rust TreeCore backend used `benchmark/engine_steps/bench_engine_steps.py` from #46006 at `ede3f52b3ffe5bd1ec13eaa848ba0e570fa24742`. ABBA means:\n\n| Baseline (ms/step) | Reuse (ms/step) | Throughput change (%) |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n| 359.435 | 359.607 | -0.048 |\n\nAll harness and engine-log checks passed. The difference is within the baseline variation of 0.168%; no stable engine-step gain or regression was established.\n\nHistorical prefill-serving screens used a different harness and the Python TreeCore fallback:\n\n| Screen | Total-token throughput change (%) |\n|---|---:|\n| 1 | +10.16 |\n| 2 | +7.32 |\n\nThese historical results are not #46006 measurements. They include cached input tokens and changing request/cache mixes, and do not establish benefit with the default Rust backend or application E2E performance. Stronger numerical qualification remains outstanding.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format with pre-commit and follow SGLang code style.\n- [ ] Complete accuracy qualification and demonstrate reproducible performance benefit.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39773615627](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39773615627)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39773615478](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39773615478)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39773615561](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39773615561)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
